! C2H8O3 | IRC (forward) | wB97X-D/6-21G+(d,p)
! Forward direction from the genuine, unconstrained saddle point located
! in aa001d.log (NSERCH=8, SADDLE POINT LOCATED, exactly one imaginary
! frequency 1360.89i, all six trans/rot modes cleanly at 0.00). Geometry
! and Hessian both taken from aa001d directly: the Hessian is the second,
! unlabeled $HESS block from aa001d.dat (confirmed genuine and final by a
! tiny-gradient $GRAD block immediately preceding it, and confirmed NOT
! the "CAUTION, APPROXIMATE HESSIAN!" block that appeared earlier in the
! same file from an intermediate step).
!
! $IRC settings (SADDLE=.t., TSENGY=.t., NPOINT=200, STRIDE=0.1,
! OPTTOL=0.00005) follow the proven working recipe from the earlier
! chloroacetaldehyde IRC run (caa005bTSaIRCb.inp), adjusted only for
! direction (FORWRD=.t. here; that reference file was FORWRD=.f.,
! i.e. backward).
!
! One deliberate change from the historical reference: $FORCE uses
! PURIFY=.t. here rather than PROJCT=.t. The aa001c/aa001d work
! established directly (via docs-input.txt) that PURIFY is the correct
! $FORCE-level keyword for cleaning up translation/rotation contamination
! when a $ZMAT is in use (PROJCT is $STATPT's own, Cartesian-specific
! keyword, not $FORCE's) -- the historical reference file may have
! carried this same unnoticed issue, since it wasn't the focus of that
! run. Whether $FORCE is even substantively invoked during RUNTYP=IRC is
! not fully certain either way; kept for consistency with the working
! reference file's structure.

 $BASIS GBASIS=N21 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 DIFFSP=.t. $END
 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=IRC NZVAR=33 $END
 $CONTRL DFTTYP=wB97X-D $END
 $IRC saddle=.t. tsengy=.t. forwrd=.t. $END
 $IRC npoint=200 stride=0.1 opttol=0.00005 $END
 $SCF DIIS=.t. DAMP=.t. $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.t. AUTO=.t. $END
 $ZMAT NONVDW(1)=8,13, 10,7, 7,3, 8,10 $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PURIFY=.t. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=25 MEMDDI=24 $END
!$CONTRL EXETYP=CHECK $END

 $DATA
